  "title": "Percutaneous Coronary Intervention (PCI) with Drug-Eluting Stents",
  "jurisdiction": "Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) LCD",
  "effective_date": "2023-01-01",
  "category": "Interventional Cardiology",
  "description": "Medicare coverage guidelines for elective percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) with drug-eluting stents. Requires coronary angiographic stenosis >= 70% in a major epicardial vessel (or FFR <= 0.80 / iFR <= 0.89 for 50-69% lesions), with limiting Canadian Cardiovascular Society (CCS) Class II-IV angina refractory to medical therapy.",
